{"kind":"assert","text":"Amendment to this request (Hugh, 17:05 Eastern), required for item 1:\n(a) Enforce user verification: dap's verifier must check the authenticator's user-verified (UV) flag and refuse an assertion without it, so a tap without biometrics or PIN never counts as a person deciding. Witness: a UV=0 assertion over the exact intent hash is refused by name.\n(b) Enrollment: a passkey is enrolled to a member by an act signed by an existing key of that same member, under a fresh check. The membership scope records the credential ID and public key (and algorithm), so the record alone can verify later assertions; revoking a passkey follows the never-remove-the-last-credential rule.\n(c) Domain in the record: each passkey-signed act records the relying-party ID (domain) and origin it was made for, and verification checks them against the enrolled credential, so portability limits are explicit rather than a surprise. The preparation note states what happens to approvals when a room moves to another host or domain."}